messages:
evan: Quick thread — post-CDN + pipeline tweak we're seeing anchors fail because some headings are emitted as percent-encoded ids (e.g. id=\"getting%20started\") while the nav links use hyphen slugs (#getting-started). Repro: /tutorials/quickstart#getting-started
linkbot: [linkcheck] ⚠ 7 anchor mismatches found. Example: /tutorials/quickstart#getting-started -> 404. CI job: https://ci.redwood.ai/teams/docs/15001
maria: Can you paste the generated HTML snippet?
evan: Sure — page has `<h2 id=\"getting%20started\">Getting Started</h2>` while sidebar uses `<a href=\"/tutorials/quickstart/#getting-started\">Getting Started</a>`. Some clients drop the fragment when they hit the CDN edge redirect.
jun: Sounds like our mdx/md pipeline started url-encoding header ids in one stage, while the slugifier used earlier replaced spaces with hyphens. Likely an ordering/regression in the new build step.
ops-bot: [deploy] Staging shows anchor failures. Proposing a short client-side shim to normalize ids at runtime so fragments resolve immediately while we fix the build.
maria: I wrote a tiny DOM shim to map decoded ids to canonical hyphen slugs and pushed it as a minimal injection in the page footer. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/800

```js
// map percent-encoded ids -> slugified hyphen ids (temporary hotpatch)
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function(){
  document.querySelectorAll('[id]').forEach(function(el){
    var id = el.id;
    try{
      var dec = decodeURIComponent(id);
    }catch(e){
      return;
    }
    var slug = dec.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/(^-|-$)/g,'');
    if(slug !== id && !document.getElementById(slug)){
      el.id = slug;
    }
  });
});
```

evan: Also relaxed linkcheck temporarily to treat percent-encoded vs hyphenated fragments as equivalent for the CI run so we don't block the release. Added mobile UA run too.
jun: Long-term fix: revert the plugin ordering and make slugification deterministic across all pipeline stages. Filing DOCS-435 to track.
ops-bot: [ci] Job 15004: staging passed after client shim + linkcheck relax.
maria: I'll add a short note in the changelog for integrators about heading id normalization and update contributing docs so new PRs run the slug regression tests.
evan: Closing thread — followups moved to DOCS-435 and PR 800. Thanks all :white_check_mark:
